{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mind Projection Fallacy.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mind Projection Fallacy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mind projection fallacy mind projection fallacy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mind Projection Fallacy.md","fileName":"Mind Projection Fallacy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mind Projection Fallacy","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Probability Interpretation and Uncertainty]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Interpretation and Uncertainty","bayesianprogramming.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mind Projection Fallacy.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mind Projection Fallacy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mind projection fallacy mind projection fallacy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mind Projection Fallacy.md","fileName":"Mind Projection Fallacy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mind Projection Fallacy","heading":"Mind Projection Fallacy","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The mind projection fallacy occurs when uncertainty in a modeler's knowledge is projected onto the external phenomenon as though the uncertainty were a property of the thing itself. A probability assignment then appears to describe inherent randomness rather than a conditional state of information.\n\nKeeping preliminary knowledge explicit avoids this confusion. The distribution states what can be inferred under a description, while the phenomenon may contain unmodeled structure that different evidence could reveal.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Interpretation and Uncertainty","bayesianprogramming.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mind Projection Fallacy.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mind P